To run the website on your local browser:

Setup (one-time):

1.  Open the siliconprep folder in VSCode (File → Open Folder)
2.  Click the Extensions icon in the left sidebar (or Ctrl+Shift+X / Cmd+Shift+X)
3.  Search for "Live Server" (by Ritwick Dey) → click Install

Running it:

1.  Right-click index.html in the file explorer → Open with Live Server
2. our browser opens automatically at something like http://127.0.0.1:5500/index.html
3.  Edit any file, hit save — the browser tab refreshes on its own. No need to re-run anything.

A "Go Live" button also appears in the bottom-right status bar of VSCode once it's installed — click it any time to start/stop the server.

A couple of things specific to this project:

-   To see the problems list or a problem page, just navigate to problems.html or problem.html in the browser (or right-click those files → Open with Live Server directly)
-   problem.html needs internet access on first load — it pulls CodeMirror (the code editor) from a CDN, so the editor won't render if you're offline

If you don't want to install anything: you can just double-click index.html in your file explorer to open it directly in a browser. That works fine for index.html and problems.html. The only downside is no auto-refresh — you'd hit refresh manually after every change, and depending on your browser, opening files with file:// links can occasionally be picky about local scripts (Live Server avoids that entirely by serving over http://), so Live Server is the more reliable option.